ps://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-165#how-interfaces-are-identified[ERC section] to learn more about how these ids are created. This function call must use less than 30 000 gas."}},"title":"VisaEscrow","version":1},"userdoc":{"kind":"user","methods":{"GRACE_PERIOD()":{"notice":"Grace period after a milestone deadline before the migrant may reclaim."},"RELAYER_ROLE()":{"notice":"Role held by the server-side relayer wallet. Can anchor agreements, submit proofs, complete milestones, pause/resume the clock, and trigger licence-revocation refunds. It CANNOT move funds arbitrarily and CANNOT block `reclaimTranche` or `claimUnresponsive` — those are callable by the migrant and adviser respectively, with no relayer gate in between."},"UNRESPONSIVE_PERIOD()":{"notice":"How long the clock must sit paused (ball in the migrant's court) before the adviser may claim the tranche as unresponsive."},"anchorAgreement(uint256,bytes32)":{"notice":"Anchors the sha256 hash of the signed fee agreement PDF. Called by the relayer once Lumin confirms both parties have signed."},"claimUnresponsive(uint256)":{"notice":"Adviser claims the current tranche when the clock has sat paused (ball in the migrant's court) for at least `UNRESPONSIVE_PERIOD` with no resume."},"completeMilestone(uint256)":{"notice":"Releases the current tranche to the adviser once proof has been submitted and the milestone's deadline has not passed. Opens the next milestone, or ends the engagement if this was the last one."},"createEngagement(address,bytes32,uint256[],uint64[])":{"notice":"Creates a new engagement. Caller becomes the migrant."},"fund(uint256)":{"notice":"Migrant pulls their tokens into escrow. Reverts unless the agreement has been anchored — money cannot move before a real signature event."},"getMilestones(uint256)":{"notice":"Returns every milestone for an engagement."},"pauseClock(uint256)":{"notice":"Pauses the current milestone's deadline clock — ball moves to the migrant's court (e.g. documents outstanding)."},"reclaimTranche(uint256)":{"notice":"Migrant reclaims all unreleased funds after the current milestone's deadline plus the grace period has passed. A deliberate claim, not an auto-sweep — the engagement ends and nobody, including the relayer, can stop it."},"refundAll(uint256)":{"notice":"Refunds all unreleased funds to the migrant and ends the engagement. Called by the relayer when the adviser's IAA licence check fails."},"resumeClock(uint256)":{"notice":"Resumes a paused clock, pushing the deadline forward by the paused duration so the adviser is not penalised for the migrant's delay."},"submitProof(uint256,bytes32)":{"notice":"Records evidence (a hash) that the current milestone's action happened. Does not move funds — `completeMilestone` does that."},"token()":{"notice":"The token this escrow holds. MockNZDD on testnet, dNZD in production."}},"notice":"Milestone escrow for New Zealand immigration adviser fees. Holds a generic IERC20 token (MockNZDD on testnet, dNZD in production — same code, no hardcoded token address) and releases it in tranches against milestones that a licensed immigration adviser and their migrant client agree to up front.","version":1}},"settings":{"compilationTarget":{"project/contracts/VisaEscrow.sol":"VisaEscrow"},"evmVersion":"prague","libraries":{},"metadata":{"bytecodeHash":"ipfs","useLiteralContent":true},"optimizer":{"enabled":true,"runs":200},"remappings":["project/:@openzeppelin/contracts/=npm/@openzeppelin/contracts@5.6.1/"]},"sources":{"npm/@openzeppelin/contracts@5.6.1/access/AccessControl.sol":{"content":"// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
